Chapter: OscNoiseTest
  cites Signal chapter Oscillator

 The mixer. `osc-noise-val` was `phase * 1103515245 + 12345` and then a
 remainder by 2000, with no downward fold. Multiplication carries entropy
 upward only, so the sample value was driven by the low bits of the phase.

 The deeper one. `osc-eval` hands `phase` to the noise branch exactly as it
 does to sine and square, and `osc-phase-at` wraps at 6283, so phase repeats
 every sample-rate/freq samples. A noise value that is a pure function of
 phase therefore repeats on the same period as the pitch. That is not a
 broken random number generator; it is a periodic waveform wearing the name
 noise, and no improvement to the mixer can fix it, because the input itself
 comes back around.

Section: Fixtures

 8000 Hz at 100 Hz gives a period of exactly 80 samples.

  ont-rate : Integer
  ont-rate = 8000

  ont-freq : Integer
  ont-freq = 100

  ont-period : Integer
  ont-period = 80

  ont-samples : Integer
  ont-samples = 240

  ont-bank : OscBank
  ont-bank = osc-add (osc-bank-new ont-rate) ont-freq 1000 osc-type-noise 0

Section: Measurement

  ont-repeats : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ont-repeats (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let a = list-at xs i
    in let b = list-at xs (i + ont-period)
    in ont-repeats xs (i + 1) n (acc + (if a == b then 1 else 0))

  ont-seen-before : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  ont-seen-before (xs) (i) (j) =
    if j >= i then False
    else if list-at xs j == list-at xs i then True
    else ont-seen-before xs i (j + 1)

  ont-distinct : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ont-distinct (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ont-distinct xs (i + 1) n (acc + (if ont-seen-before xs i 0 then 0 else 1))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let xs = osc-bank-render ont-bank ont-samples
    in let reps = ont-repeats xs 0 (ont-samples - ont-period) 0
    in let dist = ont-distinct xs 0 ont-samples 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("samples:       " & show ont-samples)
      print-line-uni ("period:        " & show ont-period)
      print-line-uni ("repeats:       " & show reps & " of " & show (ont-samples - ont-period))
      print-line-uni ("distinct:      " & show dist)
      print-line-uni ("not periodic:  " & show (reps < ont-samples - ont-period))
      print-line-uni ("above period:  " & show (dist > ont-period))
    end
